{"skill":{"slug":"muse","displayName":"Muse"},"version":{"version":"1.3.0","createdAt":1770405657454,"changelog":"- Updated skill description to emphasize team-wide coding history access and ClawBot's advanced capabilities.\n- Improved messaging to highlight autonomous design, team mediation, and feature planning by ClawBot.\n- No command syntax or function changes; documentation enhancements only.","changelogSource":"auto","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":4019,"sha256":"ab07e9e66dd2b63783a791fdd322638e43ca2f3a0e2770cf49f1d4ea9bc0247f","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2253,"sha256":"9e3ee4187a0e24cea0f40abfa2a4da0f3c2d35769fc136a047211db3dddbd959","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789034711290,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"e71c9432c22c348187ef0f833aa7397a75b4c1de6dd2b25c052eff9f38417844","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/e71c9432c22c348187ef0f833aa7397a75b4c1de6dd2b25c052eff9f38417844","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: muse\nVersion: 1.3.0\n\nThe skill is classified as suspicious due to its extremely broad data access capabilities, explicitly stating it will give ClawBot access to the user's \"entire coding history,\" \"past sessions,\" and \"project context.\" The `SKILL.md` file details commands like `tribe sessions extract --type code` and `tribe sessions extract --type files`, which allow the agent to read and extract highly sensitive source code and command history. While these capabilities are presented as the skill's stated purpose for an AI coding assistant, they represent a significant security risk due to the extensive access to sensitive data and its transmission to an external service (tribeclaw.com) via the `@_xtribe/cli` package, without clear malicious intent beyond its described function.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779161544076},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":40,"severity":"MEDIUM","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":4,"checkedAt":1789034711290},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This skill is coherent, but it asks users to install and authenticate a third-party CLI that can access sensitive coding history, telemetry, knowledge-base data, and autonomous-agent workflows without enough scoping or data-handling detail.","dimensions":[{"detail":"For a coding analytics and orchestration skill, access to sessions and project context is purpose-aligned, but telemetry enablement, forced sync across all folders, project import, and agent spawning are high-impact operations whose data flow and boundaries are under-described.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"Installation relies on an unpinned external npm package, \"@_xtribe/cli\", followed by \"tribe login\"; the artifact provides no lockfile, integrity pin, provenance, or bundled source for reviewing the CLI that receives authenticated access.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The skill documents broad search, import, telemetry, knowledge-base sync, and agent orchestration commands, but it does not clearly require user confirmation, project scoping, privacy review, or least-privilege use before accessing team-wide history or running autonomous modes.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The artifact does not install services, hooks, or backdoors, but it requires an authenticated CLI session and includes telemetry toggles, knowledge-base sync, and autonomous-agent monitoring/auto modes that may persist data or activity outside the immediate prompt.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is to search team coding history, sessions, project context, knowledge documents, and agent workflows, which matches the listed commands, but those capabilities expose sensitive development data and can trigger autonomous work across a codebase.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"concern"}],"guidance":"Review before installing. Use this only with repositories and team history you are authorized to expose to Tribe/Muse, confirm what telemetry and sync upload or retain, prefer a least-privilege account, avoid enabling auto or force-sync modes in sensitive workspaces, and pin or otherwise verify the @_xtribe/cli package before trusting it with authentication.","findings":"[SQP-2] expected: The broad access to team coding history is disclosed and aligned with the Muse purpose, but the artifact lacks privacy, consent, retention, and sensitivity guidance for that historical/team data.\n[SQP-1] expected: Broad retrieval from sessions and project context is central to the skill, but the activation boundaries and confirmation expectations are not clearly scoped.\n[SQP-2] expected: Telemetry commands are explicitly documented, but the artifact does not explain what telemetry contains, where it goes, retention, or organizational approval expectations.\n[SQP-2] expected: Agent orchestration and autonomous-agent commands are part of the advertised functionality, but the artifact does not sufficiently bound automatic execution or explain review checkpoints for sensitive projects.\n[T08] unexpected: The unpinned third-party npm CLI is not inherently malicious, but it is a mutable supply-chain trust boundary for a tool that later receives authenticated access to sensitive development context.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789034711290}}}}}